 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S447-001\", \"clauses\": {\"add\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F20\", \"template\": \"{a_numerator}/{a_denominator} {v} {b_numerator}/{b_denominator}\", \"reasoning\": \"F20 prints an addend, a plus sign from the add and subtract signs domain, and a second addend, so it produces addition problems. Its v slot is not linked to the operation, so the same family also yields subtraction problems, which is the defect recorded under overall.\"}, \"subtract\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F20\", \"template\": \"{a_numerator}/{a_denominator} {v} {b_numerator}/{b_denominator}\", \"reasoning\": \"F20 prints a minus sign from the add and subtract signs domain with two fractions, so it produces subtraction problems. The v slot is unlinked to the operation, so the family also prints the wrong sign for addition problems.\"}, \"similar_fractions\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F20\", \"template\": \"{a_numerator}/{a_denominator} {v} {b_numerator}/{b_denominator}\", \"reasoning\": \"F20 prints two fractions with the denominator keys a_den and b_den, both drawn from 4 to 6, 8, 10. Declared bounds fix the fraction type to similar_proper, so the two fractions share a denominator and the family addresses similar fractions.\"}, \"models\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F19\", \"template\": \"Shade the shape to show the result of {fraction_str}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F19 asks the learner to shade a shape, which is an area model. The declared variants include area_model, number_line and set_model, and F19 is the only family that prints a model instruction, so the representation clause is addressed through the area model.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F06\", \"F09\", \"F20\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"When {verb} {frac_lbl}s with the same {den_lbl}, keep the {den_lbl} the same.\", \"{replace} only the {num_lbl}s: {a_num} {sign} {b_num} = {step}.\", \"{a_numerator}/{a_denominator} {v} {b_numerator}/{b_denominator}\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F09 fills replace (Add or Subtract) and sign (+ or -) from independent generator choices, while step is the generated result_num, which ranges from 1 to 6 for both operations. The domains therefore allow a hint whose verb or sign contradicts the operation, and some combinations are false equations, for example a minus sign with a result larger than the first numerator. F06 chooses the verb (adding or subtracting) from the two operation verbs with no derivation from the operation, so a subtraction problem can print the hint about adding fractions. F20 chooses v (+ or -) from the add and subtract signs with no derivation from the operation, even though its template is chosen by operation. F19 prints F20 as its fraction_str and asks the learner to shade the result of that expression, so a subtraction sign in an addition problem makes the question state the wrong operation. The remaining families (F01, F02, F03, F04, F05, F07, F08, F10 to F18, F21 to F25) are not shown to produce false statements from the declared domains, and F12 and F19 carry no conflicting vocabulary. The vocabulary gates (denominator, fraction, numerator) and the vocabulary in the templates (fractions, same denominator, numerators, improper fraction) are within cumulative_vocab, and no NOT_YET_KNOWN term appears.\"}",
